Package: NilpotentMinimum
Type: Package
Title: Basic R Functionality for (Strong and Weak) Nilpotent Minimum fuzzy logics
Version: 0.1.0
Author: Igor Yegin [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Igor Yegin <igor.yegin@stir.ac.uk>
Description: (Strong) Nilpotent Minimum (commonly shortened to NM) is a class of t-norms 
    introduced by Fodor (1995) and later generalised as Weak Nilpotent Minimum (WNM) by 
    Esteva and Godo (2001). This package provides a number of R functions for a 
    flexible class of (W)NM fuzzy logics. 
    The syntax is designed to resemble that of lfl package. 
Imports: matrixStats
License: GPL (>=3)
Encoding: UTF-8
LazyData: true
URL: https://github.com/igoryegin/NilpotentMinimum
BugReports: https://github.com/igoryegin/NilpotentMinimum/issues
RoxygenNote: 7.3.3
